<section class="three-tool-knowledge" id="qurbani-deep-guide">
<h2>Qurbani share calculator: cow, camel, sheep and complete Udhiyah guide</h2>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> A sheep or goat typically counts as <strong>one sacrificial share</strong>. A cow, buffalo or camel may be divided into up to <strong>seven religious shares</strong> under common juristic guidance. <a href="https://sunnah.com/muslim:1318a" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sahih Muslim 1318a</a> records seven people sharing a camel or cow in a sacrificial Hady context. The tool separates <strong>reserving seventh-shares</strong> from <strong>splitting the price of an entire animal</strong> and does not decide intentions or religious validity.</p>
